From: Anthony Liu <anthony.liu@mediatek.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:05:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mt76: fix buffer overrun in pkt buffer

Upstream: https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/6a9b493f14946857dc37cdd2384692cffe546c92
Fixes: d4e5ca3483a0 ("wifi: mt76: mt7928: makes struct beacon_tlv 4-byte aligned.")
Signed-off-by: Anthony Liu <anthony.liu@mediatek.com>
Reported-by: kernel test robot <lkp@intel.com>
Reported-by: Dan Carpenter <error27@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Dan Carpenter <error27@gmail.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/bb9c40516e7379bf763b1ba7cec228c354494223.1793351111.git.anthony.liu@mediatek.com
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>

diff --git a/mt7925/mcu.c b/mt7925/mcu.c
index f347e1d..dc9c45d 100644
--- a/mt7925/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7925/mcu.c
@@ -2537,7 +2537,7 @@ mt7925_mcu_uni_add_beacon_offload(struct mt792x_dev *dev,
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
-	if (skb->len > 512) {
+	if (skb->len > sizeof(req.beacon_tlv.pkt)) {
 		dev_err(dev->mt76.dev, "beacon size limit exceed\n");
 		dev_kfree_skb(skb);
 		return -EINVAL;
